      "problem": "Factor $81{n}^{3}+24.$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}+{b}^{3}=(a+b)({a}^{2}-ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that all of the terms have a common factor of $3.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the $3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n81{n}^{3}+24=3(27{n}^{3}+8)\n$$\n\nThe expression in parentheses can be written as a sum of cubes:\n\n$$\n3(27{n}^{3}+8)=3((3n)^{3}+{2}^{3})\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression in parentheses using the sum of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}81{n}^{3}+24 & =3((3n)^{3}+{2}^{3}) \\\\  & =3(3n+2)((3n)^{2}-3n\\cdot 2+{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =3(3n+2)(9{n}^{2}-6n+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
