      "problem": "Factor the expression $\\frac{{x}^{3}}{8}-\\frac{{z}^{6}}{125}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}-{b}^{3}=(a-b)({a}^{2}+ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a difference of cubes:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}}{8}-\\frac{{z}^{6}}{125}={(\\frac{x}{2})}^{3}-{(\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5})}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the given expression using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{8}-\\frac{{z}^{6}}{125} & ={(\\frac{x}{2})}^{3}-{(\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5})}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5})({(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{x}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{z}^{2}}{5}+{(\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5})}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5})(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{x{z}^{2}}{10}+\\frac{{z}^{4}}{25})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
