      "name": null,
      "problem": "Factor $8+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}+{b}^{3}=(a+b)({a}^{2}-ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a sum of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n8+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}={2}^{3}+{(\\frac{1}{x})}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the sum of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}} & ={2}^{3}+{(\\frac{1}{x})}^{3} \\\\  & =(2+\\frac{1}{x})({2}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+{(\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}) \\\\  & =(2+\\frac{1}{x})(4-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
